    "because": "C10 — a unit-carrying value is `{ value, unit }` and a bare number written over one inherits the existing unit (node.ts :341-348, :1031-1040). Two Logs pass Value straight through: the object arrives downstream intact, and the later plain 5 arrives as { value: 5, unit: 'px' }. This is the behaviour NSP-011 §6 row C6 met on Value Changed and R7 asks about: C10 wrote it down as a clause; R7 (a) would narrow its second sentence to ports that declare units.",
